From: Ely Office
Subject: LOK: Impress empties slides by index as one undo step

- Linking a slide to a live scoreboard (#135) emptied it by marking
  and deleting its objects, up to three passes per slide, because a
  deleted filled placeholder leaves an empty one. Each pass was its
  own undo step, so one undo did not bring the slides back.
- .uno:ElyClearSlides takes Slides, slide indexes with ";" between,
  and removes every object but comments from them inside one undo
  group; placeholders go too. A text edit ends first and marks are
  cleared; the view keeps its slide. An index out of range, repeated
  or malformed changes nothing.

